# Line endings
#
# WHY THIS IS HERE
# ----------------
# Prettier is configured with `endOfLine: "lf"`, and `npm run lint` runs Prettier
# as an ESLint rule with `--max-warnings=0`. On Windows, a clone with the default
# `core.autocrlf=true` checks every file out with CRLF, so `lint` failed on all
# ~60 source files with "Delete `␍`" before a single line of code was written.
# CI on Linux passed, which is what let it go unnoticed.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the WORKING TREE to LF on every platform, so the bytes on disk
# match what Prettier expects regardless of a contributor's git configuration.
# Nothing about the committed content changes: git already normalised these files
# to LF on commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
